The text of the Basic Laws of Israel in this repository is not protected by copyright. Copyright Act, 5768-2007,
section 6: "Copyright shall not subsist in statutes, regulations, Knesset Records and judicial decisions of courts or
of any governmental entity having judicial authority." The text was copied from Hebrew Wikisource
(https://he.wikisource.org/), which is credited as the source of the bytes.

The catalogue facts (titles, dates and identifiers of Israeli Basic Laws) come from Wikidata, which is dedicated to the
public domain under CC0 1.0: https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/ (https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q2368137,
retrieved 30 October 2026). The treaty actions are facts recorded by the UN Treaty Collection (https://treaties.un.org/).

Lexifina's own contributions (the arrangement of the history, the commit messages, the tables and the
tools) are dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal: https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/
